          "text": "The pattern is consistent with the cubic **Y\u2083Au\u2083Sb\u2084 structure type**, space group **I-43d (No. 220)**. The principal reflections index as 211, 220, 310, 321, 420, \u2026 with \\(a \\approx 9.4641\\) \u00c5. There are four U\u2083Cu\u2083Sb\u2084 formula units per conventional cell.\n\nThe only variable positional parameter is \\(x_{\\mathrm{Sb}}\\); the powder intensities support approximately 0.083, while a full profile refinement would be needed for higher precision.\n\n```cif\ndata_U3Cu3Sb4\n_audit_creation_method              'Structure solution from Cu Kalpha1 powder XRD'\n_chemical_name_common               'U3Cu3Sb4'\n_chemical_formula_structural        'U3Cu3Sb4'\n_chemical_formula_sum               'U12 Cu12 Sb16'\n_cell_formula_units_Z               4\n\n_cell_length_a                      9.4641(5)\n_cell_length_b                      9.4641(5)\n_cell_length_c                      9.4641(5)\n_cell_angle_alpha                   90\n_cell_angle_beta                    90\n_cell_angle_gamma                   90\n_cell_volume                        847.69\n\n_space_group_crystal_system         cubic\n_space_group_name_H-M_alt           'I -4 3 d'\n_space_group_IT_number              220\n\n_diffrn_radiation_type              'Cu Kalpha1'\n_diffrn_radiation_wavelength        1.5406\n\nloop_\n_atom_site_label\n_atom_site_type_symbol\n_atom_site_symmetry_multiplicity\n_atom_site_Wyckoff_symbol\n_atom_site_fract_x\n_atom_site_fract_y\n_atom_site_fract_z\n_atom_site_occupancy\nU1   U    12  a   0.375000  0.000000  0.250000  1.0\nCu1  Cu   12  b   0.875000  0.000000  0.250000  1.0\nSb1  Sb   16  c   0.0830    0.0830    0.0830    1.0\n```\n\nRepresentative indexing:\n\n| 2\u03b8 observed (\u00b0) | hkl |\n|---:|:---|\n| 23.00 | 211 |\n| 26.62 | 220 |\n| 29.83 | 310 |\n| 35.46 | 321 |\n| 42.69 | 420 |\n| 44.89 | 332 |\n| 47.00 | 422 |\n| 49.04 | 431 |\n| 52.95 | 521 |\n| 60.23 | 611 |\n| 61.96 | 620 |\n| 63.67 | 541 |\n\nNo comparably plausible surviving alternative is required; swapping U and Cu between 12a and 12b is inconsistent with the characteristic intensity distribution and with the established U\u2083Cu\u2083Sb\u2084/Y\u2083Au\u2083Sb\u2084 topology.",
